    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d708">

                <pb facs="0765" n="755" xml:id="pg755"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">102.1/4–749: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cabot</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-04-08T18:00:00-05:00">April 8, 1949—6 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>623. For Parker from Treas. FRBNY received telegraphic request Apr 8 from China
                    CenBank to purchase another 100,000 ounces gold. Request under consideration.
                    Received urtel 1112 Apr 7 request immediate comment. Your stated assumption
                    reftel on basis Deptel 565<anchor n="44" xml:id="d708-f1"/> unclear to us but
                    will attempt defer decision until receipt advice from you. [Treasury.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
